1
00:01:39,859 --> 00:01:41,349
What are you doing there, fella?

2
00:01:44,863 --> 00:01:46,558
I just cut these.

3
00:01:49,568 --> 00:01:50,864
You better come along with us.

4
00:02:10,758 --> 00:02:12,384
Taking it off here, Boss.

5
00:02:13,092 --> 00:02:14,753
Yeah, take it off, Dragline.

6
00:02:23,103 --> 00:02:25,594
-Wiping it off here, Boss? -All right, Koko, wipe it off.

7
00:02:26,407 --> 00:02:28,101
Drinking it up here, Boss.

8
00:02:28,777 --> 00:02:30,676
All right, drink it up, Gambler.

9
00:03:03,813 --> 00:03:05,440
You eyeballing there, Society?

10
00:03:05,815 --> 00:03:07,146
Checking my yo-yo, Boss.

11
00:03:19,329 --> 00:03:20,659
Drag, new-meat bus.

12
00:03:26,837 --> 00:03:29,328
Bunch. Must be half a dozen new-meat.

13
00:03:32,843 --> 00:03:34,470
No more than five, for a cold drink.

14
00:04:15,387 --> 00:04:17,218
All right, you men get lined up there.

15
00:04:18,725 --> 00:04:20,716
Dogboy, shut them dogs up.

16
00:04:21,227 --> 00:04:23,388
They just smell new-meat, s'all, Boss.

17
00:04:30,537 --> 00:04:32,401
What did they bring us today?

18
00:04:38,545 --> 00:04:42,241
Gibson, 507 manslaughter.

19
00:04:42,917 --> 00:04:44,543
Good for a two spot.

20
00:04:45,252 --> 00:04:47,185
It was an accident. I've never been in trouble before.

21
00:04:47,254 --> 00:04:48,550
You call the Captain, "Captain."

22
00:04:48,924 --> 00:04:52,256
Edgar Potter, 302 and resisting arrest.

23
00:04:53,260 --> 00:04:54,420
One year.

24
00:04:54,763 --> 00:04:56,627
I was trying to keep in out of the rain.

25
00:04:58,066 --> 00:05:00,557
Get the wax out of your ears. You call the Captain, "Captain."

26
00:05:01,770 --> 00:05:03,760
And you call the rest of us "Boss," you hear?

27
00:05:04,941 --> 00:05:08,273
This man is going to make us proud of him, Mr. Hunnicutt.

28
00:05:09,879 --> 00:05:11,175
Raymond Pratt.

29
00:05:12,081 --> 00:05:13,069
Yes, Captain.

30
00:05:13,449 --> 00:05:15,576
Breaking, entering, and assault.

31
00:05:16,285 --> 00:05:17,581
Five spot.

32
00:05:18,187 --> 00:05:19,050
And a seaman.

33
00:05:20,289 --> 00:05:22,621
'Spect that should come in real handy around here, Captain.

34
00:05:23,292 --> 00:05:24,223
Maybe.

35
00:05:24,560 --> 00:05:26,187
Lucas Jackson.

36
00:05:26,696 --> 00:05:27,458
Here, Captain.

37
00:05:27,596 --> 00:05:31,293
Maliciously destroying municipal property while under the influence.

38
00:05:31,600 --> 00:05:33,090
What was that?

39
00:05:35,105 --> 00:05:37,095
Cutting the heads off parking meters, Captain.

40
00:05:40,811 --> 00:05:42,438
We ain't never had one of them before.

41
00:05:42,512 --> 00:05:44,206
Where do you think that's going to get you?

42
00:05:44,982 --> 00:05:46,813
I guess you could say I wasn't thinking, Captain.

43
00:05:49,820 --> 00:05:52,311
It says here that you did real good in the war.

44
00:05:52,622 --> 00:05:55,614
A Silver Star, Bronze Star, couple of Purple Hearts...

45
00:05:56,995 --> 00:05:59,623
...Sergeant. Then came out the same way you went in.

46
00:06:00,631 --> 00:06:01,825
Buck Private.

47
00:06:02,633 --> 00:06:05,032
Like I was just passing time, Captain.

48
00:06:06,505 --> 00:06:09,633
Well, you got yourself some time now...two years.

49
00:06:11,509 --> 00:06:12,840
Well, hell, that ain't much.

50
00:06:12,911 --> 00:06:15,504
We got a couple of men here doing 20 spots.

51
00:06:15,848 --> 00:06:18,009
We got one that's got all of it.

52
00:06:18,516 --> 00:06:22,350
We got all kinds, and you're going to fit in real good.

53
00:06:23,022 --> 00:06:25,855
Of course, in case you get rabbit in your blood...

54
00:06:26,158 --> 00:06:30,151
...and you decide to take off for home, you get a bonus of some time...

55
00:06:30,863 --> 00:06:33,661
...and a set of leg chains to keep you slowed down just a little bit.

56
00:06:34,166 --> 00:06:37,658
For your own good, you'll learn the rules.

57
00:06:39,672 --> 00:06:41,662
It's all up to you.

58
00:06:42,876 --> 00:06:47,540
Now I can be a good guy or I can be one real mean son of a bitch.

59
00:06:52,686 --> 00:06:55,177
It's all up to you.

60
00:06:56,190 --> 00:06:57,452
All right, let's move it.

61
00:07:15,277 --> 00:07:16,301
One at a time. Move it!

62
00:07:28,723 --> 00:07:30,247
Them clothes got laundry numbers on them.

63
00:07:30,325 --> 00:07:32,656
You remember your number and always wear the ones that has your number.

64
00:07:32,727 --> 00:07:34,922
Any man forgets his number spends a night in the box.

65
00:07:35,231 --> 00:07:37,324
These here spoons you keep with you.

66
00:07:37,533 --> 00:07:39,728
Any man loses his spoon spends a night in the box.

67
00:07:40,103 --> 00:07:42,094
There's no playing grab-ass or fighting in the building.

68
00:07:42,438 --> 00:07:44,929
You got a grudge against another man, you fight him Saturday afternoon.

69
00:07:45,241 --> 00:07:48,107
Any man playing grab-ass or fighting in the building spends a night in the box.

70
00:07:48,612 --> 00:07:51,740
First bell's at five minutes of eight when you will get in your bunk.

71
00:07:52,115 --> 00:07:53,240
Last bell is at eight.

72
00:07:53,517 --> 00:07:56,246
Any man not in his bunk at eight spends the night in the box.

73
00:07:56,620 --> 00:07:58,520
There is no smoking in the prone position in bed.

74
00:07:58,622 --> 00:08:01,249
To smoke you must have both legs over the side of your bunk.

75
00:08:01,625 --> 00:08:03,717
Any man caught smoking prone in bed...

76
00:08:03,795 --> 00:08:04,954
...spends a night in the box.

77
00:08:05,462 --> 00:08:06,450
You get two sheets.

78
00:08:06,763 --> 00:08:08,696
Every Saturday, you put the clean sheet on the top...

79
00:08:08,765 --> 00:08:10,130
...the top sheet on the bottom...

80
00:08:10,300 --> 00:08:12,131
...the bottom sheet you turn in to the laundry boy.

81
00:08:12,470 --> 00:08:14,630
Any man turns in the wrong sheet spends a night in the box.

82
00:08:14,972 --> 00:08:16,963
No one'll sit in the bunks with dirty pants on.

83
00:08:17,275 --> 00:08:20,266
Any man with dirty pants on sitting on the bunks spends a night in the box.

84
00:08:20,778 --> 00:08:23,473
Any man don't bring back his empty pop bottle spends a night in the box.

85
00:08:23,781 --> 00:08:26,272
Any man loud talking spends a night in the box.

86
00:08:27,152 --> 00:08:29,279
You got questions, you come to me.

87
00:08:30,288 --> 00:08:33,655
I'm Carr, the floor walker. I'm responsible for order in here.

88
00:08:34,493 --> 00:08:36,154
Any man don't keep order spends a night in...

89
00:08:36,495 --> 00:08:37,483
...the box.

90
00:08:39,165 --> 00:08:41,292
I hope you ain't going to be a hard case.

91
00:08:52,011 --> 00:08:54,240
Ain't but four. What did I tell you? You owe me a cold drink.

92
00:08:54,313 --> 00:08:55,302
I owe you. I owe you.

93
00:09:02,522 --> 00:09:04,683
Hey, any of you guys from Connecticut?

94
00:09:06,793 --> 00:09:07,760
Forget it.

95
00:09:08,128 --> 00:09:09,618
Wash them up!

96
00:09:11,032 --> 00:09:12,465
Wash them up!

97
00:09:22,210 --> 00:09:25,201
Well, what are you still doing here? Get at them beans!

98
00:09:42,030 --> 00:09:43,792
Next time you stay out of my place.

99
00:09:43,967 --> 00:09:45,866
You try that again and I'll bounce you off the floor.

100
00:09:46,201 --> 00:09:48,192
Well, man, I didn't know it was your special seat.

101
00:09:48,538 --> 00:09:50,028
You don't take another man's seat, man.

102
00:09:50,372 --> 00:09:51,963
It wasn't his fault. Nobody said anything...

103
00:09:52,040 --> 00:09:55,373
You better mind you manners, boy. You're acting like a hillbilly tramp.

104
00:09:55,845 --> 00:09:57,506
"Tramp." There you go, Beauty.

105
00:09:58,047 --> 00:10:00,208
Hey, yeah, man, you got your bull-gang name now.

106
00:10:00,883 --> 00:10:03,044
Yeah, well, it ain't no worse than some I been called.

107
00:10:03,720 --> 00:10:05,017
When I was in the Navy...

108
00:10:05,088 --> 00:10:06,077
All you new-meats...

109
00:10:06,389 --> 00:10:09,016
...you're going to have to shape up fast and hard for this gang.

110
00:10:09,092 --> 00:10:10,388
We got rules here.

111
00:10:10,494 --> 00:10:11,392
In order to learn them...

112
00:10:11,461 --> 00:10:13,827
...you gotta do more work with your ears than your mouth.

113
00:10:16,400 --> 00:10:17,388
Somebody say something?

114
00:10:18,568 --> 00:10:20,229
No, I didn't say nothing, Boss.

115
00:10:21,171 --> 00:10:22,160
What have we got there?

116
00:10:22,740 --> 00:10:24,071
Got a Lucas Jackson.

117
00:10:25,743 --> 00:10:28,075
You don't have a name here until Dragline gives you one.

118
00:10:29,546 --> 00:10:33,538
Maybe we ought to call it No-Ears. You don't listen much, do you, boy?

119
00:10:33,584 --> 00:10:35,484
I ain't heard that much worth listening to.

120
00:10:35,586 --> 00:10:38,077
A lot of guys laying down a lot of rules and regulations.

121
00:10:41,259 --> 00:10:42,749
New-meat looks like a poker player, Drag.

122
00:10:44,696 --> 00:10:46,357
Yeah, that wouldn't surprise me none.

123
00:10:46,431 --> 00:10:48,228
I know you've got five dollars pocket money.

124
00:10:48,300 --> 00:10:50,928
That would buy you a whole fistful of cards. You in or out?

125
00:10:52,104 --> 00:10:53,092
Out.

126
00:11:06,619 --> 00:11:07,608
First bell.

127
00:11:18,131 --> 00:11:19,290
How'd you get that scar?

128
00:11:19,633 --> 00:11:20,622
What scar?

129
00:11:22,803 --> 00:11:23,791
Last bell.

130
00:11:24,137 --> 00:11:25,297
Last bell.

131
00:11:56,505 --> 00:11:57,664
Fifty, Boss.

132
00:11:58,340 --> 00:11:59,500
Right, Carr. Fifty.

133
00:12:10,853 --> 00:12:11,842
Getting up here, Carr.

134
00:13:35,776 --> 00:13:38,768
Get out of my eyeballing seat, you new-meat dummy.

135
00:14:10,478 --> 00:14:13,811
I'm a salesman. I used to drive these roads all the time.

136
00:14:15,149 --> 00:14:16,980
Drag, it's going to be one hot mother today.

137
00:14:18,821 --> 00:14:21,312
Yeah, I reckon the Bear's going to be walking the road today.

138
00:14:21,657 --> 00:14:23,488
Then I'm lucky I got me a broom.

139
00:14:23,826 --> 00:14:28,159
I work on top, real cush job. I would hate to be down in that ditch today.

140
00:14:28,497 --> 00:14:29,656
We work in a ditch?

141
00:14:31,333 --> 00:14:32,322
What's the matter with you?

142
00:14:32,669 --> 00:14:35,831
All your big-time driving around, you never seen a chain gang before?

143
00:14:36,506 --> 00:14:39,497
I ain't used to hard work, neither. I always tried to avoid it.

144
00:14:40,009 --> 00:14:42,000
I ain't exactly crazy about it, myself.

145
00:14:42,845 --> 00:14:45,508
Well, man, it's going to be one tough day to learn on.

146
00:14:48,351 --> 00:14:50,444
Why don't you give one of these new-meat a break...

147
00:14:50,520 --> 00:14:52,010
...and let him use your broom today?

148
00:14:52,355 --> 00:14:55,188
Oh, hell, Society, I ain't going down in that ditch.

149
00:14:55,526 --> 00:14:58,688
Well, I sure would appreciate it. I ain't in too good a shape right now.

150
00:14:59,029 --> 00:15:01,691
Hey, Koko, you really going to sell your job?

151
00:15:02,033 --> 00:15:03,523
Well, Drag, I may have to.

152
00:15:04,535 --> 00:15:06,695
Maybe that Lucas War Hero would give you your price.

153
00:15:07,038 --> 00:15:08,528
I'll give you 50 cents.

154
00:15:08,873 --> 00:15:12,536
Fifty cents for a sweet job like that? That's worth at least a buck.

155
00:15:13,210 --> 00:15:14,198
I'll make it a dollar.

156
00:15:14,546 --> 00:15:15,534
Dollar's a deal.

157
00:15:20,218 --> 00:15:22,378
Where'd you get that about war hero?

158
00:15:22,720 --> 00:15:24,688
A little birdie told me.

159
00:15:24,756 --> 00:15:26,518
Tearing the heads off of...what was it?

160
00:15:26,725 --> 00:15:28,215
Gumball machines?

161
00:15:28,760 --> 00:15:31,251
What kind of thing is that for a grown man?

162
00:15:33,065 --> 00:15:36,557
You know how it is. Small town. Not much to do in the evening.

163
00:15:38,570 --> 00:15:40,731
Mostly was just settling an old score.

164
00:15:57,590 --> 00:16:00,423
Boss, I made this arrangement with this man to take his broom.

165
00:16:04,932 --> 00:16:06,922
-You don't understand, I made this deal. -Get moving.

166
00:16:08,102 --> 00:16:09,432
But I made this arrangement.

167
00:16:13,440 --> 00:16:14,771
Get to work.

168
00:16:34,295 --> 00:16:37,753
Better take it easy. You won't last two hours.

169
00:16:41,136 --> 00:16:42,797
Taking it off here, Boss?

170
00:16:43,138 --> 00:16:45,129
Yeah, Dragline, take it off there.

171
00:16:45,174 --> 00:16:47,437
-Taking it off here, Boss? -Take it off.

172
00:16:49,478 --> 00:16:50,467
Drinking it up here, Boss?

173
00:17:05,829 --> 00:17:07,159
Man bear-clawed here, Boss!

174
00:17:31,022 --> 00:17:32,046
All right, men.

175
00:17:32,524 --> 00:17:34,014
Let's eat them beans!

176
00:17:50,042 --> 00:17:51,532
Cold drink he don't make it.

177
00:17:54,213 --> 00:17:55,305
He won't.

178
00:17:55,548 --> 00:17:57,538
Hey, Babalugats, got a bet here.

179
00:18:22,510 --> 00:18:25,842
-Boss, drinking it up here. -Right.

180
00:18:31,485 --> 00:18:32,474
Who's that?

181
00:18:33,187 --> 00:18:34,175
That's Godfrey.

182
00:18:35,157 --> 00:18:36,316
The Walking Boss.

183
00:18:49,504 --> 00:18:50,664
Don't he ever talk?

184
00:18:55,443 --> 00:18:57,104
Think he just said somethin'.

185
00:19:33,718 --> 00:19:35,878
You owe that fella a cold drink.

186
00:19:51,903 --> 00:19:52,733
All right!

187
00:19:53,238 --> 00:19:55,637
You, Gibson, step out.

188
00:19:57,243 --> 00:19:59,574
Boss Paul says you wasn't happy with your job.

189
00:20:00,412 --> 00:20:01,571
Says you was complaining.

190
00:20:02,414 --> 00:20:04,905
Well, we going to give you a chance to think about it.

191
00:20:05,417 --> 00:20:06,405
All right.

192
00:20:06,552 --> 00:20:07,917
Let's go.

193
00:20:16,762 --> 00:20:18,093
Get them clothes off.

194
00:21:16,792 --> 00:21:17,781
First bell.

195
00:21:20,663 --> 00:21:25,157
Plumb busted out. Looks like the hard road finally got to Mr. Lucas War Hero.

196
00:21:25,835 --> 00:21:27,995
I'll be back at it in the morning. Just need a little nap.

197
00:21:28,338 --> 00:21:30,829
Man, I never thought they'd put him in the box on his first day.

198
00:21:32,175 --> 00:21:33,665
It was only supposed to be a joke.

199
00:21:35,345 --> 00:21:36,835
There ain't no brooms.

200
00:21:37,180 --> 00:21:39,171
Well, can't expect to learn everything the first day.

201
00:21:40,684 --> 00:21:42,674
They've taught him a very valuable lesson.

202
00:21:45,189 --> 00:21:47,180
You guys sure give him all night to think about it.

203
00:21:48,025 --> 00:21:50,357
We can't help it if he's square. Huh, Drag?

204
00:21:51,028 --> 00:21:55,362
Of course not. He ain't in the box because of a joke played on him.

205
00:21:56,033 --> 00:21:58,194
He back-sassed a free man.

206
00:21:58,870 --> 00:22:01,532
They got their rules and we ain't got nothing to do with that.

207
00:22:02,707 --> 00:22:06,039
Probably happen to him sooner or later anyway, complainer like him.

208
00:22:06,877 --> 00:22:09,710
He's gotta learn the rules, same as anybody else.

209
00:22:11,216 --> 00:22:13,878
Yeah, them poor old bosses need all the help they can get.

210
00:22:15,220 --> 00:22:16,209
Trying to say something?

211
00:22:22,194 --> 00:22:23,319
Last bell!

212
00:22:24,764 --> 00:22:25,889
Last bell!

213
00:22:27,732 --> 00:22:30,064
One of these days I'm gonna have to flap me up some dust with it.

214
00:22:30,569 --> 00:22:36,131
-Forty-nine and one in the box, Boss. -Right, Carr, 49 and one in the box.

215
00:23:08,342 --> 00:23:09,638
Putting them on here, Boss.

216
00:23:12,281 --> 00:23:13,771
You see that, you see that?

217
00:23:13,848 --> 00:23:15,075
I got eyes, don't I?

218
00:23:15,149 --> 00:23:17,844
How am I not going to see someone that looks like that?

219
00:23:21,790 --> 00:23:23,280
Man, oh, man, look at that. Look at that!

220
00:23:32,835 --> 00:23:34,996
-Wipin' it off here, Boss. -Wipe it off.

221
00:23:43,780 --> 00:23:45,576
-Taking them off here, Boss? -All right.

222
00:23:46,649 --> 00:23:48,640
Damn thing's blocking the scenery.

223
00:23:52,322 --> 00:23:54,984
Oh man, I'm dying. I'm dying!

224
00:24:03,100 --> 00:24:04,430
Nice broad.

225
00:24:06,770 --> 00:24:07,758
Great set.

226
00:24:17,048 --> 00:24:19,675
Lucille, baby.

227
00:24:29,594 --> 00:24:32,722
Oh man, I'm dying! I'm dying!

228
00:24:36,702 --> 00:24:40,536
She ain't got nothing, but...one safety pin holding that thing on!

229
00:24:42,542 --> 00:24:45,033
Come on, safety pin, pop!

230
00:24:48,246 --> 00:24:49,577
C'mon baby, pop!

231
00:24:52,552 --> 00:24:53,540
Hey, Lord...

232
00:24:54,053 --> 00:24:57,386
...whatever I done, don't strike me blind for another couple of minutes.

233
00:24:59,892 --> 00:25:01,382
My Lucille.

234
00:25:03,564 --> 00:25:05,724
Your Lucille, boy. Where did you get that?

235
00:25:06,567 --> 00:25:08,057
That's Lucille, you mother-head.

236
00:25:08,569 --> 00:25:11,731
Anything so innocent, and built like that...

237
00:25:12,072 --> 00:25:13,733
...just gotta be named Lucille.

238
00:25:16,376 --> 00:25:18,936
Rub it, baby. Clean that car.

239
00:25:19,012 --> 00:25:21,003
Rub...rub...

240
00:25:50,613 --> 00:25:52,604
She don't know what she's doing.

241
00:25:53,283 --> 00:25:55,614
Oh boy, she knows exactly what she's doing.

242
00:25:55,951 --> 00:25:58,442
She's driving us crazy, and loving every minute of it!

243
00:25:59,455 --> 00:26:01,787
Shut your mouth about my Lucille.

244
00:26:29,487 --> 00:26:30,818
Shut up, Babalugats.

245
00:26:31,156 --> 00:26:32,588
You leave him alone? He's happy.

246
00:26:32,657 --> 00:26:33,987
Because he's a damn moron!

247
00:28:04,453 --> 00:28:06,114
Oh, man, that little Lucille.

248
00:28:06,822 --> 00:28:10,622
She was really a big lot of little gal, wasn't she?

249
00:28:13,329 --> 00:28:17,322
Did you see how she was just about popping out of the top of that dress?

250
00:28:17,967 --> 00:28:19,457
Come on, Drag, cut it out.

251
00:28:20,637 --> 00:28:22,127
And down below...

252
00:28:22,839 --> 00:28:25,466
...man, that thing didn't reach no higher than...

253
00:28:29,479 --> 00:28:32,141
She's liable to catch a cold running around like that.

254
00:28:33,350 --> 00:28:36,842
It was stretched so tight across her bottom...

255
00:28:37,354 --> 00:28:41,290
...I do believe I saw one of those seams bust loose.

256
00:28:42,660 --> 00:28:44,650
And the opening got wider...

257
00:28:45,863 --> 00:28:47,159
...and wider...and wider.

258
00:28:49,666 --> 00:28:50,655
Forget it, man.

259
00:28:53,171 --> 00:28:54,365
What do you mean, forget it?

260
00:28:55,673 --> 00:28:59,507
Stop beating it into the ground. You ain't doing nobody no good.

261
00:29:02,181 --> 00:29:05,014
Okay, new-meat. You get some sleep.

262
00:29:06,385 --> 00:29:08,512
And save your strength, 'cause you're going to need it.

263
00:29:11,390 --> 00:29:12,379
Tomorrow.

264
00:30:45,789 --> 00:30:47,279
Why don't you just stay down, Luke?

265
00:30:47,357 --> 00:30:49,119
He's just going to knock you down again, buddy.

266
00:30:49,493 --> 00:30:51,120
It's not your fault. He's just too big.

267
00:30:51,495 --> 00:30:53,656
Let him hit you in the nose and get some blood flowing.

268
00:30:53,797 --> 00:30:55,628
Maybe the bosses'll stop it before he kills you.

269
00:30:55,999 --> 00:30:57,295
I don't want to frighten him.

270
00:30:57,768 --> 00:30:58,893
Stay down, Luke.

271
00:31:01,806 --> 00:31:04,797
Stay down, Luke. He's gonna kill you.

272
00:31:47,454 --> 00:31:48,442
Stay down!

273
00:32:06,574 --> 00:32:09,065
Somebody ought to stop this thing.

274
00:32:50,619 --> 00:32:51,744
Stay down.

275
00:32:52,422 --> 00:32:53,411
You're beat!

276
00:32:55,425 --> 00:32:56,915
You're going to have to kill me.

277
00:34:07,968 --> 00:34:09,333
All right, pass right. Here we go.

278
00:34:09,503 --> 00:34:13,997
King gets a three, queen deuce, seven pair of savannah's right here.

279
00:34:14,341 --> 00:34:17,332
Deuce gets a four. No hell. Three gets a big ace.

280
00:34:23,850 --> 00:34:24,839
I call.

281
00:34:36,531 --> 00:34:37,589
Kick a buck.

282
00:34:37,665 --> 00:34:38,961
A dollar?

283
00:34:42,037 --> 00:34:43,937
One time.

284
00:34:44,373 --> 00:34:45,930
All right, I'll call.

285
00:34:46,508 --> 00:34:48,703
Hell, if I catch, I'm gonna burn you out. I call.

286
00:34:49,544 --> 00:34:52,377
King, three, he got a four. Queen, deuce gets a five.

287
00:34:52,581 --> 00:34:54,548
Pair of seven gets a john.

288
00:34:54,583 --> 00:34:57,380
And the big ace gets...slop in the face.

289
00:34:59,054 --> 00:35:01,249
Okay, you still do the talking.

290
00:35:02,257 --> 00:35:03,245
Cuter again.

291
00:35:03,960 --> 00:35:04,948
I call.

292
00:35:08,331 --> 00:35:09,319
Kick a buck.

293
00:35:12,535 --> 00:35:14,196
-What you got? -Pair of sevens.

294
00:35:14,270 --> 00:35:17,261
I can see that, mother-head. What have you got in the hole?

295
00:35:19,576 --> 00:35:21,567
He ain't got nothing showing. Raze his head off.

296
00:35:21,978 --> 00:35:22,967
He's been betting...

297
00:35:23,180 --> 00:35:25,147
All right, why don't you call him.

298
00:35:27,284 --> 00:35:29,274
You've got to see it, Gambler.

299
00:35:29,587 --> 00:35:31,520
I can't. I can't catch a damn thing...

300
00:35:31,589 --> 00:35:33,580
I'm snake-bit. I fold.

301
00:35:35,292 --> 00:35:38,591
King, four, three. You got a nine. You got a nine. Nothing visible.

302
00:35:39,297 --> 00:35:41,457
Pair of sevens and a jack gets a six.

303
00:35:42,266 --> 00:35:44,325
Savannahs, you still a better, man.

304
00:35:52,043 --> 00:35:53,031
Kick a buck.

305
00:35:53,445 --> 00:35:55,003
Kick him back a buck!

306
00:35:55,113 --> 00:35:57,445
I'll see your buck and back a buck.

307
00:35:59,985 --> 00:36:00,973
Kick a buck.

308
00:36:01,053 --> 00:36:01,984
Damn!

309
00:36:02,087 --> 00:36:03,452
Don't look at me, mother-head.

310
00:36:06,958 --> 00:36:09,620
What're you going to do, play like a coconut? You got to call him.

311
00:36:10,830 --> 00:36:13,458
I know he's got a pair of kings. You don't have to stuff'em up my nose.

312
00:36:13,833 --> 00:36:15,460
Well, you still got to call him, anyway.

313
00:36:17,637 --> 00:36:19,433
The man's got kings. Get your tail out.

314
00:36:23,911 --> 00:36:25,901
You wanna see him? Right there.

315
00:36:32,152 --> 00:36:34,143
Nothing. Handful of nothing.

316
00:36:34,488 --> 00:36:36,979
You stupid mullet-head, he beat you with nothing.

317
00:36:37,591 --> 00:36:41,254
Just like today when he kept coming back at me. With nothing.

318
00:36:45,666 --> 00:36:47,998
Sometimes nothing can be a real cool hand.

319
00:36:52,373 --> 00:36:53,362
Move over.

320
00:36:54,008 --> 00:36:56,374
I'm going to sit in here next to my boy.

321
00:36:58,680 --> 00:37:00,375
Cool Hand Luke.

322
00:37:25,641 --> 00:37:26,665
Hey, Loudmouth!

323
00:37:27,610 --> 00:37:30,272
Come on, get up there. Your mama's waiting for you.

324
00:37:32,716 --> 00:37:34,206
She never leaves me alone!

325
00:37:35,051 --> 00:37:36,915
Be glad you got somebody, kid.

326
00:37:37,221 --> 00:37:39,211
Luke, visitor for you.

327
00:38:14,693 --> 00:38:16,854
-Coming out here, Boss. -Come out, Luke.

328
00:39:08,483 --> 00:39:09,507
How did you find me?

329
00:39:10,051 --> 00:39:12,713
That Helen...

330
00:39:13,088 --> 00:39:15,420
...she sent your things along with a note...

331
00:39:15,757 --> 00:39:19,591
...and then John here, he wrote to the police.

332
00:39:25,266 --> 00:39:26,596
Goin' around here, Boss?

333
00:39:30,939 --> 00:39:32,600
Well, Arletta, I've got to stay here.

334
00:39:36,946 --> 00:39:39,278
I always hoped to see you well-fixed...

335
00:39:40,449 --> 00:39:44,112
...have me a crop of grandkids to fuss around with.

336
00:39:45,622 --> 00:39:47,749
I'd like to oblige you, Arletta, but...

337
00:39:47,957 --> 00:39:50,289
...right off, I just don't know where to put my hands on 'em.

338
00:39:54,297 --> 00:39:55,627
You know, sometimes...

339
00:39:56,634 --> 00:39:59,296
...I wish people was like dogs, Luke.

340
00:40:01,972 --> 00:40:04,964
Comes a time, a day like when...

341
00:40:06,144 --> 00:40:09,636
...the bitch just don't recognize the pups no more, so...

342
00:40:11,983 --> 00:40:16,477
...she don't have no hopes, nor love to give her pain.

343
00:40:19,490 --> 00:40:21,152
She just don't give a damn.

344
00:40:26,331 --> 00:40:27,821
They letting you smoke here?

345
00:40:28,333 --> 00:40:29,663
Smoking it up here, Boss?

346
00:40:38,344 --> 00:40:39,674
You done your best, Arletta.

347
00:40:43,849 --> 00:40:45,578
What I've done with myself is my own problem.

348
00:40:45,684 --> 00:40:49,518
Oh, no, it ain't, Luke. You ain't alone.

349
00:40:50,190 --> 00:40:52,521
Everywhere you go, I'm with you.

350
00:40:53,693 --> 00:40:55,024
And John, too.

351
00:40:57,697 --> 00:40:59,528
You never thought maybe that's a heavy load?

352
00:41:01,475 --> 00:41:05,639
Why, we always thought you were strong enough to carry it.

353
00:41:08,709 --> 00:41:10,039
Was we wrong?

354
00:41:10,376 --> 00:41:11,365
I don't know.

355
00:41:14,181 --> 00:41:15,579
Well, things are just never the way...

356
00:41:15,649 --> 00:41:16,980
...they seem, Arletta, you know that.

357
00:41:17,051 --> 00:41:18,541
A man's gotta go his own way.

358
00:41:19,054 --> 00:41:20,544
Guess, I've just got to...

359
00:41:22,556 --> 00:41:24,387
...got to love you and let go.

360
00:41:27,061 --> 00:41:27,720
I guess.

361
00:41:30,899 --> 00:41:33,390
I ain't asking what you're going to do when you get out because...

362
00:41:33,735 --> 00:41:36,568
...l'll be dead and it don't matter.

363
00:41:40,910 --> 00:41:42,672
You never did want to live forever.

364
00:41:42,745 --> 00:41:44,576
I mean, it wasn't such a hell of a life.

365
00:41:46,248 --> 00:41:49,581
I had me...some high old times.

366
00:41:50,252 --> 00:41:51,742
Your old man, Luke...

367
00:41:52,588 --> 00:41:54,748
...he wasn't much good for sticking around...

368
00:41:55,091 --> 00:41:58,083
...but, dammit, he made me laugh.

369
00:42:01,598 --> 00:42:03,929
I would have liked to have known him, the way you talk about him.

370
00:42:15,612 --> 00:42:17,102
He'd have broke you up.

371
00:42:34,631 --> 00:42:36,292
What went wrong?

372
00:42:36,634 --> 00:42:38,966
Nothing. Everything's cool as can be.

373
00:42:41,806 --> 00:42:43,467
Arletta, I tried.

374
00:42:44,642 --> 00:42:45,631
I mean to...

375
00:42:47,812 --> 00:42:49,973
...live always free and above board like you, but...

376
00:42:51,317 --> 00:42:53,648
...I don't know, I just can't seem to find any elbow room.

377
00:42:58,991 --> 00:43:01,322
You always had good jobs.

378
00:43:02,329 --> 00:43:05,320
And that girl in Kentucky.

379
00:43:05,664 --> 00:43:08,827
Oh...l'd taken a shine to her.

380
00:43:09,336 --> 00:43:12,999
She sure took off with that convertible fella.

381
00:43:13,340 --> 00:43:14,670
Well, why not?

382
00:43:15,508 --> 00:43:19,842
Idea of marrying got you all, all bollixed up.

383
00:43:22,015 --> 00:43:24,175
Trying to be respectable.

384
00:43:25,518 --> 00:43:28,851
You was boring the hell out of all of us.

385
00:43:39,201 --> 00:43:40,862
I'm leaving the place to John.

386
00:43:41,203 --> 00:43:42,191
That's good. He earned it.

387
00:43:43,204 --> 00:43:44,695
Ain't nothing to do with it.

388
00:43:48,542 --> 00:43:50,373
I just never gave John...

389
00:43:52,547 --> 00:43:55,380
...the kind of, you know, feeling that I gave you.

390
00:43:55,717 --> 00:43:59,209
So, I'm going to pay him back now.

391
00:44:01,289 --> 00:44:04,281
Don't feel you have to say anything.

392
00:44:07,062 --> 00:44:09,053
The way it is, you see...

393
00:44:14,737 --> 00:44:19,070
...sometimes you just have a feeling for a child...

394
00:44:21,077 --> 00:44:22,408
...or else you don't.

395
00:44:24,247 --> 00:44:26,238
With John, I just didn't.

396
00:44:32,589 --> 00:44:33,919
I gotta go, Arletta.

397
00:44:36,093 --> 00:44:38,755
Laugh it up, kid. You, you'll make out.

398
00:44:49,441 --> 00:44:52,773
Uncle Luke, why can't you have chains?

399
00:44:55,113 --> 00:44:57,206
John-Boy, let me tell you something.

400
00:44:57,282 --> 00:45:00,614
You know them chains ain't medals. You got them for making mistakes.

401
00:45:01,553 --> 00:45:05,249
And you make a bad enough mistake, then you've got to deal with the Man.

402
00:45:05,957 --> 00:45:07,788
And he is one rough old boy.

403
00:45:22,541 --> 00:45:24,532
So long, Arletta. Take care.

404
00:45:25,312 --> 00:45:26,642
You know it, kid.

405
00:45:31,318 --> 00:45:33,149
Now there ain't nothing to come back for.

406
00:45:40,327 --> 00:45:44,660
"Just a closer walk with Thee.

407
00:45:48,336 --> 00:45:53,000
"Grant it, Jesus, is my plea.

408
00:45:56,511 --> 00:46:01,175
"Daily walking close to Thee.

409
00:46:04,685 --> 00:46:08,018
"Let it be, dear Lord...

410
00:46:08,356 --> 00:46:10,517
"...let it be.

411
00:46:13,862 --> 00:46:18,356
"Through the days of toil that's near...

412
00:46:20,869 --> 00:46:25,533
"...if I fall, dear Lord, who cares?

413
00:46:30,046 --> 00:46:32,537
"Who but Thee...

414
00:46:32,882 --> 00:46:35,544
"...my burden shares?

415
00:46:37,220 --> 00:46:38,881
"None but Thee...

416
00:46:39,489 --> 00:46:42,822
"...dear Lord, none but Thee!"

417
00:47:08,919 --> 00:47:11,080
This gang's been doing so good...

418
00:47:12,424 --> 00:47:14,915
...the Captain decided to give you something special.

419
00:47:17,394 --> 00:47:20,727
You've got yourselves a whole road of tarring to do.

420
00:47:22,934 --> 00:47:24,765
And I want to see you roll it.

421
00:47:30,610 --> 00:47:32,100
Pick up your shovels.

422
00:47:32,777 --> 00:47:34,438
Get with it. Move!

423
00:47:38,117 --> 00:47:40,050
We're sure going to be walking the road today.

424
00:47:40,119 --> 00:47:41,279
What's the deal?

425
00:47:41,454 --> 00:47:45,288
-Man, you think you been working hard? -This mother's going to break your back.

426
00:48:26,902 --> 00:48:28,733
Let's move! Let's see those shovels!

427
00:48:33,241 --> 00:48:37,575
Going to twist my arm off if it don't kill me first. Right, Boss?

428
00:48:46,088 --> 00:48:48,249
Hey, buddy, slow down.

429
00:48:49,091 --> 00:48:50,581
That's a long road.

430
00:48:52,595 --> 00:48:56,258
Well, the man wants speed, let's just give it to him.

431
00:48:56,933 --> 00:49:00,925
Cram it in and break it out. Yeah. Go hard.

432
00:49:02,772 --> 00:49:04,433
What are we racing for?

433
00:49:05,608 --> 00:49:08,099
Wants speed, let's give it to him.

434
00:49:09,279 --> 00:49:11,110
Use that shovel like it was your spoon.

435
00:49:26,464 --> 00:49:28,125
The man, boy, get the man!

436
00:49:28,467 --> 00:49:29,626
Moving it up here, Boss.

437
00:50:09,176 --> 00:50:11,667
Now you tell me, Rabbit, what's going on here?

438
00:50:12,512 --> 00:50:15,175
I don't know, Boss. Think they're all bear-clawed.

439
00:50:22,689 --> 00:50:24,850
They don't know whether to smile, spit or swallow.

440
00:50:25,526 --> 00:50:28,859
Well, they've never seen a bull gang before.

441
00:51:44,108 --> 00:51:45,439
Where'd the road go?

442
00:51:46,444 --> 00:51:49,106
That's it. That's the end of it.

443
00:51:49,781 --> 00:51:51,111
Man, there's still daylight.

444
00:51:51,949 --> 00:51:53,439
About two hours left.

445
00:51:55,287 --> 00:51:56,618
What do we do now?

446
00:51:58,290 --> 00:51:59,279
Nothing.

447
00:52:00,125 --> 00:52:03,458
Oh, Luke, you wild, beautiful thing!

448
00:52:04,630 --> 00:52:06,961
You crazy handful of nothing!

449
00:52:28,154 --> 00:52:29,815
"As Carol pressed her lips to him...

450
00:52:30,491 --> 00:52:34,654
"...his right hand started a slow descent down her silken body.

451
00:52:35,662 --> 00:52:39,154
"Desire and fear, temptation and terror...

452
00:52:39,833 --> 00:52:43,667
"...yearning and horror warred within her beautiful young body."

453
00:52:45,245 --> 00:52:47,907
Have to close those things, or we'd drown,

454
00:52:49,077 --> 00:52:50,065
but it's suffocating in here.

455
00:52:51,346 --> 00:52:52,676
Talk about drowning.

456
00:52:53,847 --> 00:52:55,405
When I was in the navy...

457
00:52:55,483 --> 00:52:58,178
...I was on submarine duty once, and when you get down there...

458
00:52:58,519 --> 00:53:01,352
Will you tell your story walkin'? It's too hot.

459
00:53:11,867 --> 00:53:14,027
Did you see my skinny little boy chow tonight?

460
00:53:14,203 --> 00:53:16,034
He's matching you plate for plate.

461
00:53:16,538 --> 00:53:19,701
I wasn't feeling good. I think I got an ulcer or something.

462
00:53:21,043 --> 00:53:23,705
He had a bigger spoon. Make you look like yours had a hole in it.

463
00:53:24,380 --> 00:53:25,369
Come on, Clarence.

464
00:53:25,548 --> 00:53:28,210
What do you mean, Clarence? You call me a liar?

465
00:53:28,284 --> 00:53:29,273
No, not a liar.

466
00:53:29,352 --> 00:53:32,878
You just have a common, likeable tendency toward exaggeration.

467
00:53:36,059 --> 00:53:39,221
That there's the champion hog-gutter of this camp.

468
00:53:40,063 --> 00:53:42,223
Well, I've seen him eat ten chocolate bars...

469
00:53:42,566 --> 00:53:45,228
...and seven cold drinks in 15 minutes.

470
00:53:46,570 --> 00:53:50,563
He can eat busted bottles and rusty nails, any damn thing.

471
00:53:50,908 --> 00:53:54,240
If you be so kind to let me cut off your Yankee head, he'll even eat that.

472
00:53:56,581 --> 00:53:57,911
I can eat 50 eggs.

473
00:54:02,920 --> 00:54:04,250
Nobody can eat 50 eggs.

474
00:54:04,589 --> 00:54:05,919
You just said he could eat anything.

475
00:54:06,257 --> 00:54:07,246
You ever eat 50 eggs?

476
00:54:07,592 --> 00:54:09,423
Nobody ever eat 50 eggs.

477
00:54:09,762 --> 00:54:11,423
Hey, Babalugats! We got a bet here.

478
00:54:12,263 --> 00:54:15,255
My boy says he can eat 50 eggs, he can eat 50 eggs.

479
00:54:15,501 --> 00:54:16,364
Yeah, but in how long?

480
00:54:18,137 --> 00:54:19,296
In an hour.

481
00:54:19,438 --> 00:54:21,429
Well, I believe I'll take part in that wager.

482
00:54:21,774 --> 00:54:22,933
Two dollars. Right here.

483
00:54:23,275 --> 00:54:24,606
Come on now, let's talk some money.

484
00:54:24,943 --> 00:54:26,774
All right, $20. Anything.

485
00:54:27,112 --> 00:54:28,943
The syndicate will cover any bet you want to make.

486
00:54:29,014 --> 00:54:30,139
Koko, get some paper.

487
00:54:30,282 --> 00:54:33,615
Drag, 50 eggs got to weigh a good six pounds.

488
00:54:33,952 --> 00:54:36,944
Man's gut can't hold that. They'll swell up and bust him open.

489
00:54:37,791 --> 00:54:40,953
All right, get your money up. Now, Gambler, Dynamite, come on, get it up.

490
00:54:41,294 --> 00:54:43,956
Koko-head's going to take all the money. Come on, Loudmouth, get it up.

491
00:54:44,097 --> 00:54:45,961
Wait just a minute, now. How's he gonna eat them?

492
00:54:46,167 --> 00:54:48,498
Boiled for 15 minutes. Eat the whole thing in an hour.

493
00:54:48,802 --> 00:54:50,963
One rule. No throwing up.

494
00:54:51,337 --> 00:54:53,828
He throws up, you forfeit everything.

495
00:54:54,141 --> 00:54:56,803
Now when was the last time you ever saw my boy throw up?

496
00:54:57,144 --> 00:54:59,135
Now shut your mouth and give your money to Koko.

497
00:55:06,187 --> 00:55:08,519
Why did you have to say 50 for?

498
00:55:08,823 --> 00:55:11,986
Why couldn't you say 35 or 39.

499
00:55:12,293 --> 00:55:13,817
It seemed a nice round number.

500
00:55:14,496 --> 00:55:17,158
That's money you're talking about. What's the matter with you?

501
00:55:18,166 --> 00:55:20,828
Yeah, well, it'll be something to do.

502
00:55:27,409 --> 00:55:28,899
-Ten! -Ten, right!

503
00:55:33,215 --> 00:55:34,705
What did I do?

504
00:55:36,685 --> 00:55:38,846
I stole and I told lies.

505
00:55:41,190 --> 00:55:43,681
But I loved my neighbor. And his wife.

506
00:55:44,694 --> 00:55:45,683
He'll never make it.

507
00:55:48,865 --> 00:55:52,357
What we've got to do is stretch that little old belly of yours.

508
00:55:53,871 --> 00:55:56,202
Get all this stuff out of the way. Them eggs's coming down.

509
00:55:59,375 --> 00:56:02,344
We've got to get it all in fighting shape, like a barrage balloon.

510
00:56:07,484 --> 00:56:08,712
Ready...

511
00:56:09,486 --> 00:56:10,952
...and go!

512
00:56:21,733 --> 00:56:25,225
Hey, Boss, man needs a brown bomber and a dose of salts.

513
00:56:32,710 --> 00:56:34,337
You can't do that!

514
00:56:36,749 --> 00:56:39,615
-I want my money back. -No money back.

515
00:56:50,764 --> 00:56:53,095
Twenty of those pills still won't make any difference.

516
00:56:53,432 --> 00:56:55,263
What are you worried about? He can't do it.

517
00:56:56,735 --> 00:56:57,997
What's he doing?

518
00:57:36,945 --> 00:57:40,107
All right, stand back, you pedestrians. This ain't no automobile accident.

519
00:57:40,181 --> 00:57:41,205
That's all 50?

520
00:57:41,282 --> 00:57:43,614
Move over, losers. I got money riding here.

521
00:57:46,122 --> 00:57:47,554
All right, I've got it figured out.

522
00:57:47,623 --> 00:57:50,820
If he eats an egg a minute, he's got ten minutes left to swallow them.

523
00:57:51,127 --> 00:57:54,118
Hey, I just got five bucks from a rodeo outfit.

524
00:57:56,465 --> 00:57:58,956
-Hey, you're peeling his eggs. -That's right, mister.

525
00:57:59,469 --> 00:58:01,460
He peels his eggs himself. That's understood.

526
00:58:01,804 --> 00:58:04,534
Now you may be just great at hanging paper around the big city...

527
00:58:04,607 --> 00:58:05,630
...and passing bad checks...

528
00:58:05,976 --> 00:58:07,966
...but us country boys ain't entirely brainless.

529
00:58:08,311 --> 00:58:11,303
When it comes to the law, nothing is understood.

530
00:58:11,648 --> 00:58:13,479
Wait a minute! Wait a minute!

531
00:58:13,817 --> 00:58:16,650
Who made what law about peeling the eggs?

532
00:58:16,987 --> 00:58:19,820
I'm his trainer. I'm the syndicate covering all bets.

533
00:58:20,156 --> 00:58:22,989
And I'm his official egg-peeler. That's the law.

534
00:58:28,165 --> 00:58:29,996
Just wait till the hour starts, that's all.

535
00:58:30,334 --> 00:58:32,325
I was banking on the fact he had to peel 'em.

536
00:58:35,172 --> 00:58:36,230
What's going on?

537
00:58:46,017 --> 00:58:47,177
You ready, Champ?

538
00:58:52,892 --> 00:58:54,051
Ready?

539
00:58:55,795 --> 00:58:56,954
Go!

540
00:59:00,800 --> 00:59:01,959
Two...

541
00:59:02,401 --> 00:59:03,390
...three...

542
00:59:03,536 --> 00:59:05,867
Man, he's going to lose a finger eating eggs like that.

543
00:59:15,047 --> 00:59:16,309
Twenty-four...

544
00:59:22,088 --> 00:59:23,180
...twenty-five...

545
00:59:23,256 --> 00:59:24,245
Slow down a little.

546
00:59:29,062 --> 00:59:30,050
Twenty-six...

547
00:59:34,068 --> 00:59:35,899
Forget it, he's wasting time.

548
00:59:53,922 --> 00:59:54,910
Thirty-two.

549
01:00:00,116 --> 01:00:01,207
Just have 18 more to go...

550
01:00:02,517 --> 01:00:03,448
What's wrong?

551
01:00:03,518 --> 01:00:05,314
-I think he's gonna throw up! -Oh, no.

552
01:00:05,387 --> 01:00:07,287
-That's it. He's finished. -C'mon Luke!

553
01:00:07,322 --> 01:00:08,481
Eighteen to go.

554
01:00:11,826 --> 01:00:12,485
He's finished.

555
01:00:21,836 --> 01:00:24,828
Just like a ripe watermelon that's about to bust itself open.

556
01:00:25,173 --> 01:00:27,504
Your boy's done for, Drag. I'm putting in my last tenner.

557
01:00:27,842 --> 01:00:31,004
-lt don't look good, Drag. -Man's gut can't hold more than that.

558
01:00:40,855 --> 01:00:43,846
-He's all right, he's all right. -He's going to make it.

559
01:00:55,102 --> 01:00:58,128
I give you a dollar he don't eat all 50 eggs, I get two dollars back.

560
01:00:58,539 --> 01:01:00,530
Fixer, you're a sweet old boy.

561
01:01:00,874 --> 01:01:04,206
Better take that dollar and buy yourself a new spark plug or something.

562
01:01:04,545 --> 01:01:07,035
But as long as you done took a stand...

563
01:01:07,381 --> 01:01:10,373
...why don't you put some money where your mouth is and not no measly buck!

564
01:01:10,718 --> 01:01:12,048
Well, all I got is 3.75, Drag.

565
01:01:12,386 --> 01:01:13,717
That's a bet, Koko.

566
01:01:14,054 --> 01:01:17,080
All right, now the rest of you, I want to hear from some big-money men.

567
01:01:17,156 --> 01:01:18,555
Where's all the high rollers?

568
01:01:18,891 --> 01:01:23,225
I believe you've got it all, Dragline. Every cent in the camp is riding.

569
01:01:36,844 --> 01:01:38,834
-What's the time? -Come on, baby.

570
01:01:39,847 --> 01:01:41,676
Twenty-four minutes to go.

571
01:01:42,081 --> 01:01:46,074
Just let that little old belly sag and enjoy itself.

572
01:01:59,098 --> 01:02:00,257
Forty-one.

573
01:02:01,100 --> 01:02:05,433
Stay loose, buddy. Just nine more between you and everlasting glory.

574
01:02:05,772 --> 01:02:08,433
-ls he eating them, Alibi? -He's chewing. Look at that.

575
01:02:09,575 --> 01:02:12,441
They're pigeon eggs, that's all. Fish eggs, practically.

576
01:02:12,779 --> 01:02:13,939
How much more time, Carr?

577
01:02:14,280 --> 01:02:15,439
Six minutes to go, Stevie.

578
01:02:17,016 --> 01:02:18,744
Chew, chew, chew!

579
01:02:18,817 --> 01:02:19,977
You're helpin' him chew now!

580
01:02:20,019 --> 01:02:20,678
Oh, no.

581
01:02:23,623 --> 01:02:24,612
Forty-two.

582
01:02:27,160 --> 01:02:29,024
Tiny, tiny egg.

583
01:02:35,134 --> 01:02:36,622
Two minutes to time!

584
01:02:45,178 --> 01:02:46,166
Forty-four.

585
01:02:46,478 --> 01:02:49,641
All right, now, get mad at them damned eggs.

586
01:02:49,948 --> 01:02:50,937
Eat it there, boy.

587
01:02:51,149 --> 01:02:52,080
Chew on it.

588
01:02:52,217 --> 01:02:53,206
Gnaw on it.

589
01:02:59,257 --> 01:03:00,086
Thirty seconds.

590
01:03:01,293 --> 01:03:02,884
You got the last one.

591
01:03:03,095 --> 01:03:04,994
Stuff it down in there. Get it in.

592
01:03:05,831 --> 01:03:08,822
That's the last one in there now, baby. Chew. Chew.

593
01:03:11,703 --> 01:03:13,694
Ten...nine...eight...

594
01:03:14,706 --> 01:03:17,698
...seven...six...five...

595
01:03:18,710 --> 01:03:20,905
...four...three...two...

596
01:03:21,713 --> 01:03:23,908
...one...zero!

597
01:03:27,185 --> 01:03:28,845
Hold it! He didn't swallow the last.

598
01:03:29,554 --> 01:03:31,885
You think so? Just take a look here.

599
01:03:32,656 --> 01:03:34,145
Open that mouth.

600
01:03:50,375 --> 01:03:52,365
Nobody can eat 50 eggs.

601
01:04:11,562 --> 01:04:13,427
Snake in the grass here, Boss!

602
01:04:13,496 --> 01:04:14,929
Get it.

603
01:04:15,032 --> 01:04:16,623
Get it!

604
01:04:33,082 --> 01:04:33,946
Hey, Boss.

605
01:04:34,919 --> 01:04:36,647
Forgot your walking stick?

606
01:04:48,933 --> 01:04:50,422
Man, you sure can shoot.

607
01:04:58,776 --> 01:05:01,608
You gone too far when you mess with the Man With No Eyes.

608
01:05:02,111 --> 01:05:03,635
You'll be out of here in a little bit.

609
01:05:03,713 --> 01:05:05,407
Why don't you take it a little easy?

610
01:05:25,468 --> 01:05:27,958
All right, everybody in the trucks.

611
01:05:36,479 --> 01:05:39,139
Boy, look at Him go! Bam! Bam!

612
01:05:39,815 --> 01:05:43,808
Just knock it off, Luke! You can't talk about Him that way.

613
01:05:44,486 --> 01:05:46,716
You still believe in that big bearded Boss up there?

614
01:05:46,789 --> 01:05:47,813
You think He's watching us?

615
01:05:48,157 --> 01:05:49,487
Get in here!

616
01:05:49,858 --> 01:05:51,324
Ain't you scared?

617
01:05:52,328 --> 01:05:53,988
Ain't you scared of dying?

618
01:05:54,330 --> 01:05:56,990
Dying? Boy, He can have this little life anytime He wants to.

619
01:05:57,332 --> 01:05:59,162
You hear that? You hear it?

620
01:06:00,168 --> 01:06:03,330
Come on! You're welcome to it, Old Timer.

621
01:06:04,172 --> 01:06:06,001
Let me know You're up there. Come on.

622
01:06:06,341 --> 01:06:09,333
Love me, hate me, kill me, anything. Just let me know it.

623
01:06:14,016 --> 01:06:15,346
Just standing in the rain...

624
01:06:16,685 --> 01:06:17,673
...talking to myself.

625
01:06:23,025 --> 01:06:26,357
Blind Dick is paying back three and borrowing five.

626
01:06:26,895 --> 01:06:28,020
Next.

627
01:06:28,195 --> 01:06:29,526
You borrowing or paying back?

628
01:06:29,631 --> 01:06:30,460
Borrowing.

629
01:06:31,032 --> 01:06:34,365
Well, Mr. Cool Hand here is the soft heart in our loan department.

630
01:06:35,504 --> 01:06:36,492
I just need five, Luke.

631
01:06:39,875 --> 01:06:41,705
I knew you could really eat all them eggs.

632
01:06:42,878 --> 01:06:44,367
Yeah, well, I didn't.

633
01:06:47,548 --> 01:06:50,209
That's my darling Luke. He grins like a baby...

634
01:06:51,218 --> 01:06:52,707
...but he bites like a 'gator.

635
01:06:53,722 --> 01:06:55,211
I believe I still owe you thirty.

636
01:06:55,289 --> 01:06:56,880
I don't suppose you'd care to take a check?

637
01:07:06,099 --> 01:07:07,066
For you.

638
01:07:26,586 --> 01:07:27,917
His mother's dead.

639
01:08:20,473 --> 01:08:23,964
"I don't care if it rains or freezes...

640
01:08:24,310 --> 01:08:28,143
"...as long as I got my plastic Jesus...

641
01:08:28,481 --> 01:08:33,144
"...sitting on the dashboard of my car.

642
01:08:37,156 --> 01:08:40,989
"Comes in colors pink and pleasant.

643
01:08:41,326 --> 01:08:44,988
"Glows in the dark 'cause it's iridescent.

644
01:08:45,665 --> 01:08:48,155
"Take it with you...

645
01:08:49,502 --> 01:08:52,493
"...when you travel far.

646
01:08:55,507 --> 01:08:59,340
"Get yourself a sweet Madonna...

647
01:08:59,678 --> 01:09:03,340
"...dressed in rhinestone sittin' on...

648
01:09:04,016 --> 01:09:08,180
"...a pedestal of abalone shell.

649
01:09:11,522 --> 01:09:15,355
"Going 90, I ain't scary...

650
01:09:16,028 --> 01:09:19,690
"...'cause I got the Virgin Mary...

651
01:09:20,032 --> 01:09:22,022
"...assuring me...

652
01:09:22,700 --> 01:09:25,532
"...that I won't go to hell.

653
01:09:32,076 --> 01:09:34,908
"Get yourself a sweet Madonna...

654
01:09:35,079 --> 01:09:37,911
"...dressed in rhinestone sittin' on...

655
01:09:37,982 --> 01:09:41,917
"...pedestal of abalone shell.

656
01:09:44,188 --> 01:09:47,020
"Going 90, I ain't scary...

657
01:09:47,625 --> 01:09:51,754
"...'cause I got the Virgin Mary. assuring me...

658
01:09:52,096 --> 01:09:54,928
"...that I won't go to hell."

659
01:10:15,253 --> 01:10:16,584
Luke, fall out.

660
01:10:26,096 --> 01:10:28,428
When a man's mother dies and...

661
01:10:28,932 --> 01:10:32,925
...he gets to thinkin' about her funeral and paying respects...

662
01:10:33,771 --> 01:10:36,933
...before he knows it, his mind ain't right.

663
01:10:37,941 --> 01:10:40,602
He's got rabbit in his blood and he runs.

664
01:10:41,945 --> 01:10:43,936
We're keeping you off the road for a while.

665
01:10:51,455 --> 01:10:53,615
I'm going to say a prayer for your ma, Luke.

666
01:11:34,663 --> 01:11:38,996
Sorry, Luke, I'm just doing my job. You've got to appreciate that.

667
01:11:41,503 --> 01:11:43,664
Calling it your job don't make it right, Boss.

668
01:13:05,419 --> 01:13:08,251
Ma's in the ground now, God rest her soul.

669
01:13:09,924 --> 01:13:11,254
You best forget about it, Luke.

670
01:13:12,760 --> 01:13:16,093
Got a day and a half lay-in. Tomorrow's a holiday.

671
01:14:08,648 --> 01:14:11,172
-Happy Fourth of July! -Same to you!

672
01:14:56,862 --> 01:15:00,025
Break it up. Come on, you've had your fun.

673
01:15:00,299 --> 01:15:03,233
First bell! Move it, Stevie.

674
01:15:09,041 --> 01:15:11,031
What have you got, another one of them dirty books?

675
01:15:11,377 --> 01:15:15,039
Do yourself a favor. Read this part that Koko underlined for me.

676
01:15:18,050 --> 01:15:21,382
"She moved her head another inch while he reached up...

677
01:15:22,387 --> 01:15:24,877
"...and put his left hand on Carol's...

678
01:15:25,891 --> 01:15:27,380
"...as Carol pressed her..."

679
01:15:28,226 --> 01:15:30,217
Oh, I can't stand it!

680
01:15:32,397 --> 01:15:34,729
You're just coming to the interesting part now.

681
01:15:47,445 --> 01:15:49,777
-I can't hear you. -"Her trembling body..."

682
01:15:57,756 --> 01:16:00,588
Last bell. Last bell.

683
01:16:02,961 --> 01:16:03,790
Move it.

684
01:16:05,263 --> 01:16:06,923
What's that noise outside?

685
01:16:11,436 --> 01:16:12,424
Man on the fence, Boss!

686
01:16:25,483 --> 01:16:26,471
Wait a minute, damn it!

687
01:16:28,151 --> 01:16:29,981
Come back here! Dammit!

688
01:16:34,791 --> 01:16:38,124
Forty-eight, Boss. One in the box and one in the bush.

689
01:16:38,795 --> 01:16:42,128
Forty-eight. One in the box and one in the bush.

690
01:17:05,155 --> 01:17:06,984
Oh, listen to Blue sing!

691
01:17:08,158 --> 01:17:11,490
He's on to him, he says. He's got him.

692
01:17:11,828 --> 01:17:13,658
Hell, that dog's running around in circles.

693
01:17:13,997 --> 01:17:15,156
No, he's on to him.

694
01:17:15,666 --> 01:17:18,327
Captain says for us to wait till the patrol gets here.

695
01:17:19,168 --> 01:17:20,998
Shoulda waited for me to get him out.

696
01:17:21,070 --> 01:17:22,832
Loose like that he can run him crazy.

697
01:17:23,172 --> 01:17:26,004
Didn't even have enough sense to run from the road like everybody else.

698
01:17:26,342 --> 01:17:28,674
Oh, I'm beat. This ain't my job nohow.

699
01:18:28,404 --> 01:18:30,200
Your dogs are crazy.

700
01:18:31,907 --> 01:18:33,704
He's smarter than a dog. Let's go!

701
01:21:12,865 --> 01:21:14,059
He made it!

702
01:21:16,869 --> 01:21:18,063
Look, Captain!

703
01:21:19,205 --> 01:21:20,694
Look what he done to Blue.

704
01:21:22,208 --> 01:21:23,196
He's dead.

705
01:21:26,379 --> 01:21:28,369
He run himself plumb to death.

706
01:22:02,747 --> 01:22:04,907
Get in line facing the Captain.

707
01:22:48,659 --> 01:22:52,287
You're going to get used to wearing them chains after a while, Luke...

708
01:22:52,663 --> 01:22:55,290
...but you never stop listening to them clinking.

709
01:22:56,800 --> 01:23:00,291
'Cause they're going to remind you of what I've been saying...

710
01:23:01,472 --> 01:23:02,802
...for your own good.

711
01:23:03,674 --> 01:23:05,664
Wish you'd stop being so good to me, Captain.

712
01:23:10,314 --> 01:23:12,804
Don't you ever talk that way to me.

713
01:23:13,884 --> 01:23:14,872
Never!

714
01:23:14,952 --> 01:23:16,009
Never!

715
01:23:23,327 --> 01:23:25,816
What we've got here is...

716
01:23:26,830 --> 01:23:28,990
...failure to communicate.

717
01:23:30,333 --> 01:23:33,325
Some men you just can't reach.

718
01:23:34,337 --> 01:23:39,000
So you get what we had here last week. Which is the way he wants it.

719
01:23:39,709 --> 01:23:41,198
Well, he gets it.

720
01:23:43,847 --> 01:23:47,338
I don't like it any more than you men.

721
01:23:56,393 --> 01:23:57,882
Well, lookie here.

722
01:23:59,729 --> 01:24:01,218
I knew they'd get you.

723
01:24:01,864 --> 01:24:03,626
Them chains and a bonus of a couple of years...

724
01:24:03,700 --> 01:24:06,532
Your running days are over forever, boy.

725
01:24:07,236 --> 01:24:09,032
Hell, I'd like to see you try to run again.

726
01:24:10,373 --> 01:24:13,740
You know, you getting so you smell so bad I can track you myself.

727
01:24:15,745 --> 01:24:19,043
Yeah, well, that ought to be easy for a genuine son of a bitch.

728
01:24:31,761 --> 01:24:33,194
What happened. How far did you get?

729
01:24:33,261 --> 01:24:34,386
Shut up and let him eat.

730
01:24:35,398 --> 01:24:36,763
About a mile and a half.

731
01:24:39,901 --> 01:24:41,425
This supermarket parking lot.

732
01:24:41,536 --> 01:24:43,094
Found a car with keys in the ignition.

733
01:24:43,773 --> 01:24:46,900
Hit this red light and this police car slides up alongside.

734
01:24:49,579 --> 01:24:50,909
Then what did you do?

735
01:24:52,080 --> 01:24:53,410
Waited for that light to change.

736
01:24:55,785 --> 01:24:58,275
This cop kept looking over, wondering what somebody looks like me...

737
01:24:58,587 --> 01:25:01,419
...dressed in state issue, was doin' driving a shiny new buggy.

738
01:25:04,192 --> 01:25:06,022
So what did you do?

739
01:25:06,427 --> 01:25:09,088
He leaned over and said, "Hey!"

740
01:25:10,098 --> 01:25:12,361
Top flight police work, that's all there is to it.

741
01:25:12,501 --> 01:25:14,298
Fella's probably a lieutenant by now.

742
01:25:21,943 --> 01:25:24,809
Now, we're just gonna lay low and build time.

743
01:25:24,946 --> 01:25:27,277
Before you know it, the heat's going to be off of you.

744
01:25:27,949 --> 01:25:30,815
Everything will be right back where it was. Right, sweet buddy?

745
01:25:44,332 --> 01:25:46,629
I hear tell you don't believe in no God, Luke.

746
01:25:47,835 --> 01:25:50,565
I was wondering how come a nice, clean-cut young fellow like you...

747
01:25:51,138 --> 01:25:53,333
...gets put on the hard road.

748
01:25:54,342 --> 01:25:55,638
Now I reckon I knows.

749
01:25:57,344 --> 01:26:00,835
I've been on the road gang almost 22 years.

750
01:26:02,149 --> 01:26:04,481
In all that time, I ain't never killed a white man...

751
01:26:05,986 --> 01:26:07,646
...but I ain't afraid to because...

752
01:26:08,155 --> 01:26:10,987
Excuse me, Boss, don't mean to interrupt. Caught short here.

753
01:26:11,525 --> 01:26:13,425
So did I. It's okay.

754
01:26:14,161 --> 01:26:16,493
You just go on out there behind them trees.

755
01:26:17,164 --> 01:26:19,359
Man's gotta have his privacy sometime.

756
01:26:20,366 --> 01:26:22,856
You just keep shaking that bush so we know you're there.

757
01:26:23,671 --> 01:26:25,661
Just keep shaking that bush.

758
01:26:53,900 --> 01:26:55,197
Shaking it up here, Boss!

759
01:26:59,405 --> 01:27:00,393
Still shaking it, Boss.

760
01:27:04,711 --> 01:27:06,406
I'm shaking it, Boss.

761
01:27:30,570 --> 01:27:32,059
He's gone. Get the dogs.

762
01:28:31,796 --> 01:28:33,456
What you got them on for?

763
01:28:33,798 --> 01:28:34,958
How do you take your pants off?

764
01:28:37,035 --> 01:28:40,526
Best way is to get rid of them leg irons...

765
01:28:40,805 --> 01:28:42,136
...but you ain't strong enough.

766
01:28:42,473 --> 01:28:43,804
Strong enough for what?

767
01:28:45,810 --> 01:28:47,299
Hell, you couldn't heft an axe.

768
01:28:47,645 --> 01:28:48,474
Can, too.

769
01:28:48,813 --> 01:28:50,643
-I bet you can't. -Can, too.

770
01:28:52,116 --> 01:28:53,549
Bet you can't.

771
01:28:54,152 --> 01:28:55,812
Well, then, go get it, man.

772
01:29:02,493 --> 01:29:03,653
What's your name, boy?

773
01:29:06,163 --> 01:29:08,323
Aren't you going to take those stripes off your pants?

774
01:29:10,166 --> 01:29:11,326
You know it, kid.

775
01:29:26,517 --> 01:29:28,347
-You want to see something real funny? -Yeah?

776
01:29:28,519 --> 01:29:30,679
Well, you go on in there and you get me...

777
01:29:30,755 --> 01:29:33,018
...chili powder and pepper and the like.

778
01:29:53,209 --> 01:29:54,869
You better let me handle that, son.

779
01:30:28,310 --> 01:30:29,641
Here they are.

780
01:30:30,713 --> 01:30:31,508
Thank you, son.

781
01:30:31,580 --> 01:30:32,911
What's the matter with him?

782
01:30:33,582 --> 01:30:34,571
He'll be all right.

783
01:30:41,757 --> 01:30:44,749
Now listen. You're going to have some fun. You hear that?

784
01:30:45,095 --> 01:30:47,153
Well, you remember how them dogs do when they come through here...

785
01:30:47,229 --> 01:30:49,093
...so you can tell me about it someday, okay?

786
01:32:04,672 --> 01:32:06,663
My wife hasn't written me for a month.

787
01:32:09,509 --> 01:32:10,840
She's probably sick of you.

788
01:32:18,352 --> 01:32:19,841
Magazine for you.

789
01:32:24,358 --> 01:32:27,189
Hey, Koko, who's sending me magazines?

790
01:32:30,198 --> 01:32:31,528
Don't know. It's from Atlanta.

791
01:32:31,866 --> 01:32:32,854
My uncle!

792
01:32:33,700 --> 01:32:36,692
Ain't heard from him in eight years and now he's sending me magazines!

793
01:32:38,538 --> 01:32:40,198
He must have gone crazy!

794
01:32:45,046 --> 01:32:46,205
Look at that!

795
01:32:46,546 --> 01:32:48,537
-That's Luke? -Look at that, two of 'em.

796
01:32:51,551 --> 01:32:53,040
What's the writing say?

797
01:32:53,887 --> 01:32:55,376
What's that, that writing say?

798
01:32:55,889 --> 01:32:57,879
"Dear Boys: Playing it cool."

799
01:33:05,899 --> 01:33:07,889
They must be six feet tall.

800
01:33:14,407 --> 01:33:15,738
Look at that!

801
01:33:16,075 --> 01:33:18,043
My baby! We're in here digging and dying...

802
01:33:18,111 --> 01:33:20,578
...he's out there living and flying.

803
01:33:48,774 --> 01:33:50,263
Koko, will you stop that?

804
01:33:51,277 --> 01:33:52,937
Why don't you try making me?

805
01:34:04,623 --> 01:34:07,956
-Hey, Drag? Let me see the picture. -What for?

806
01:34:08,459 --> 01:34:10,119
Come on, Drag, let us see the picture.

807
01:34:10,461 --> 01:34:12,520
No, you're just a kid. What you know about it?

808
01:34:12,598 --> 01:34:14,394
You don't want to see that dirty picture.

809
01:34:15,134 --> 01:34:17,124
Luke and those broads and all that booze.

810
01:34:17,735 --> 01:34:19,259
Come on, let me take a look.

811
01:34:19,305 --> 01:34:21,499
It would go to your coconut head. You're liable to get ideas...

812
01:34:21,572 --> 01:34:23,232
...and pass right out.

813
01:34:24,143 --> 01:34:27,134
Now, what you figure it's worth? A peek at that there picture?

814
01:34:27,478 --> 01:34:29,810
A quick look now. I'm not talking about no memorizing job.

815
01:34:30,149 --> 01:34:31,308
Cold drink.

816
01:34:31,649 --> 01:34:33,640
A coke? One cold drink...

817
01:34:33,986 --> 01:34:37,318
...to feast your starving, fishy, little eyes on the picture?

818
01:34:37,655 --> 01:34:39,646
A true vision of paradise itself...

819
01:34:39,992 --> 01:34:42,653
...with two of the angels right there frisking around with my boy?

820
01:34:45,029 --> 01:34:46,359
Okay, it's a deal.

821
01:34:46,832 --> 01:34:48,662
One cold drink, in advance.

822
01:35:03,348 --> 01:35:05,248
One chilly bottle right in my hot little hand.

823
01:35:05,316 --> 01:35:07,806
That goes for the rest of you mother-heads, too.

824
01:35:08,619 --> 01:35:09,676
Let me see.

825
01:35:09,921 --> 01:35:11,320
Did you pay?

826
01:35:15,360 --> 01:35:16,519
Come on in there, Wicker Man.

827
01:35:46,056 --> 01:35:50,048
You run one time, you got yourself a set o' chains.

828
01:35:50,627 --> 01:35:52,788
You run twice, you get yourself two sets.

829
01:35:54,231 --> 01:35:56,027
You ain't going to need no third set...

830
01:35:56,099 --> 01:35:58,225
...because you're going to get your mind right.

831
01:35:59,569 --> 01:36:01,730
And I mean "right."

832
01:36:03,408 --> 01:36:05,398
Take a good look at Luke.

833
01:36:07,744 --> 01:36:08,733
Cool Hand Luke.

834
01:36:18,688 --> 01:36:20,621
Easy, easy! Let him breathe!

835
01:36:23,093 --> 01:36:25,253
Oh my poor baby. They done you real good.

836
01:36:26,096 --> 01:36:27,926
I don't know if you're going to have the girls chasing you.

837
01:36:27,997 --> 01:36:29,521
I'll get some aspirin.

838
01:36:29,566 --> 01:36:30,691
He should have a doctor.

839
01:36:30,767 --> 01:36:31,562
Ain't you gonna learn?

840
01:36:31,634 --> 01:36:34,330
They ain't gonna let no doctor see what they done.

841
01:36:34,437 --> 01:36:36,598
Get your razor. We'll clean up some them cuts on his head.

842
01:36:38,441 --> 01:36:41,102
How you feeling, buddy? How you feeling?

843
01:36:42,278 --> 01:36:44,939
Somebody ought to give him something cold to drink.

844
01:36:46,115 --> 01:36:48,605
-That's my baby. -Now he's going to be all right.

845
01:36:49,452 --> 01:36:52,284
Hey, Luke, look we got the picture you sent us. Look here.

846
01:36:57,794 --> 01:36:59,454
You really can pick 'em, Luke.

847
01:36:59,795 --> 01:37:02,126
Come on...tell us. What were they like?

848
01:37:02,465 --> 01:37:04,125
Can't you wait until he stops bleeding?

849
01:37:04,533 --> 01:37:07,057
-Why don't ya go back to your knitting? -Oh, knock it off, you guys.

850
01:37:07,136 --> 01:37:09,297
Picture's a phoney. Cost me a week's pay.

851
01:37:09,638 --> 01:37:10,968
What do you mean, a phoney?

852
01:37:11,307 --> 01:37:12,501
What you talking about, man?

853
01:37:12,575 --> 01:37:14,475
We saw them two women right here in the picture.

854
01:37:15,144 --> 01:37:16,974
Did you have them both at once? I mean, together?

855
01:37:17,313 --> 01:37:20,645
Picture's a phoney. I had it made up for you guys.

856
01:37:20,983 --> 01:37:22,472
What do you mean? We saw it all!

857
01:37:23,118 --> 01:37:24,277
You was having a big time, man.

858
01:37:24,386 --> 01:37:25,716
You had it made!

859
01:37:25,987 --> 01:37:28,148
Nothing. Made nothing, had nothing.

860
01:37:28,823 --> 01:37:30,653
Couple of towns, couple of bosses.

861
01:37:31,327 --> 01:37:33,487
I laughed out loud once, he turned me in.

862
01:37:33,828 --> 01:37:34,817
But I got it here!

863
01:37:35,164 --> 01:37:38,496
Oh, come on! Stop beating it!

864
01:37:39,834 --> 01:37:41,323
Get out there yourself!

865
01:37:42,837 --> 01:37:46,670
Stop feeding off me! Get outa here!

866
01:37:46,809 --> 01:37:48,571
Can't breathe. Give me some air!

867
01:37:55,683 --> 01:37:57,616
Well, he ain't himself, can't you see that?

868
01:37:57,720 --> 01:38:00,017
He's all beat up. He don't know what he's sayin'.

869
01:38:01,856 --> 01:38:04,085
All right, come on, break it up.

870
01:38:04,225 --> 01:38:05,783
Now, straighten out that bench.

871
01:38:28,215 --> 01:38:29,681
You were eyeballing.

872
01:38:29,750 --> 01:38:32,378
Can't get your mind on them weeds if you're eyeballing.

873
01:38:33,053 --> 01:38:35,714
You don't need reasons to kick me, Boss.

874
01:38:41,595 --> 01:38:43,255
First bell. Move it.

875
01:38:48,736 --> 01:38:50,066
He'll never make it.

876
01:38:50,404 --> 01:38:51,563
What are you talking about?

877
01:39:03,383 --> 01:39:06,874
That old box will collapse and fall apart before old Luke calls it quits.

878
01:39:07,220 --> 01:39:09,380
Your Luke's got more guts than brains.

879
01:39:09,723 --> 01:39:11,383
Well, I don't see no sign of guts in you.

880
01:39:11,725 --> 01:39:14,386
No. No chains, either.

881
01:39:14,728 --> 01:39:16,888
Big deal paperhanger, passing two bit checks.

882
01:39:17,229 --> 01:39:20,061
You haven't had much luck playing follow-the-leader, have you?

883
01:39:26,405 --> 01:39:28,396
You want to spend the night in the box, too?

884
01:39:33,245 --> 01:39:37,238
Well, here's our champion hog-gut. Hasn't eaten for four days.

885
01:39:37,583 --> 01:39:40,574
You're going to need a little extra. Got plenty for you.

886
01:39:40,921 --> 01:39:42,046
Now you know the rules.

887
01:39:42,189 --> 01:39:44,418
Got to clean your plate or go back to the box. Right, Boss?

888
01:39:44,758 --> 01:39:45,746
That's enough, Dogboy.

889
01:39:46,092 --> 01:39:48,083
Oh, man used to free-world food has got a big appetite.

890
01:39:48,227 --> 01:39:50,593
We're going to stretch that hog-belly right out?

891
01:41:16,781 --> 01:41:18,772
Well, you made the week, boy.

892
01:41:19,517 --> 01:41:22,509
Now you got a day and a half to rest up for old Monday.

893
01:41:52,549 --> 01:41:55,039
That ditch is Boss Kean's ditch.

894
01:41:55,720 --> 01:41:57,880
I told him that dirt in it is your dirt.

895
01:41:58,889 --> 01:42:00,880
What's your dirt doing in his ditch?

896
01:42:02,392 --> 01:42:03,551
I don't know, Boss.

897
01:42:04,728 --> 01:42:06,558
You better get in there and get it out, boy.

898
01:42:22,745 --> 01:42:26,236
"We work in the morning hear the ding-dong ring...

899
01:42:27,084 --> 01:42:30,575
"...go march to the table, see the same damn thing.

900
01:42:31,255 --> 01:42:34,917
"Well, it's on the table, a knife, a fork and a pan.

901
01:42:35,591 --> 01:42:38,924
"Say anything about it you get in trouble with the man.

902
01:42:41,597 --> 01:42:45,259
"That Midnight Special. Shine a light on me.

903
01:42:45,935 --> 01:42:49,768
"Let the Midnight Special shine your ever-loving light on me.

904
01:42:51,941 --> 01:42:55,273
"If you ever go to Houston, boy, you better walk right.

905
01:42:55,611 --> 01:42:59,604
"And you better not stagger, and you better not fight...

906
01:43:00,283 --> 01:43:02,444
"...Because the sheriff will arrest you."

907
01:43:02,785 --> 01:43:04,445
Luke, what you think you're doing?

908
01:43:07,456 --> 01:43:10,288
Just getting my dirt out of Boss Kean's ditch, Boss.

909
01:43:10,626 --> 01:43:13,458
I'm damned if you're going to put your dirt in my yard.

910
01:43:13,796 --> 01:43:15,660
You hear me?

911
01:43:15,731 --> 01:43:17,027
Now let's get it out of here.

912
01:44:00,675 --> 01:44:04,008
I told you to get your dirt out of Boss Kean's ditch, didn't I?

913
01:44:07,781 --> 01:44:08,941
Yeah, Boss.

914
01:44:09,251 --> 01:44:11,150
Then how come it ain't out?

915
01:44:17,691 --> 01:44:19,521
I don't know, Boss.

916
01:44:19,861 --> 01:44:21,521
You don't know.

917
01:44:45,053 --> 01:44:49,045
"Ain't no grave going to keep my body down.

918
01:44:51,059 --> 01:44:53,390
"Ain't no grave...

919
01:44:53,727 --> 01:44:56,718
"...going to hold my body down.

920
01:44:59,067 --> 01:45:02,557
"Keep Your mind on me above.

921
01:45:03,404 --> 01:45:06,895
"Keep Your heart full of love.

922
01:45:07,408 --> 01:45:10,899
"Ain't no grave gonna hold my body down..."

923
01:45:52,118 --> 01:45:54,108
What's all this dirt doing in here?

924
01:46:01,361 --> 01:46:03,352
I don't know...

925
01:46:14,307 --> 01:46:18,970
"When I was a little bitty baby, my mamma used to rock me in my cradle.

926
01:46:19,312 --> 01:46:22,802
"In them old cotton fields back home."

927
01:46:25,985 --> 01:46:27,315
Don't, Boss.

928
01:46:27,620 --> 01:46:28,985
Get to work.

929
01:46:29,822 --> 01:46:31,652
Don't, Boss. Don't hit me anymore.

930
01:46:34,994 --> 01:46:36,824
For God's sake, don't hit me anymore.

931
01:46:37,662 --> 01:46:41,495
What was that you said? What was that name you used, Luke?

932
01:46:43,335 --> 01:46:44,324
Oh, God!

933
01:46:46,839 --> 01:46:47,827
Oh, God!

934
01:46:53,345 --> 01:46:56,006
Oh, God, I pray to God you don't hit me anymore.

935
01:46:59,184 --> 01:47:02,176
I'll do anything you say, but I can't take anymore.

936
01:47:03,355 --> 01:47:07,017
-You got your mind right, Luke? -Yeah...

937
01:47:08,360 --> 01:47:09,520
...mind right.

938
01:47:13,365 --> 01:47:15,356
Oh, I got it right, Boss.

939
01:47:23,208 --> 01:47:24,868
Suppose you was to backslide on us?

940
01:47:25,210 --> 01:47:27,201
Oh, no, I won't, Boss.

941
01:47:28,045 --> 01:47:30,206
Suppose you was to back-sass?

942
01:47:30,714 --> 01:47:33,046
Oh, no, I won't. I won't. I got my mind right.

943
01:47:41,560 --> 01:47:43,550
You try to run again, we're going to kill you.

944
01:47:44,061 --> 01:47:45,550
I won't, I won't, Boss.

945
01:47:52,236 --> 01:47:56,569
Go get cleaned up and get yourself some sleep. Expect you need it.

946
01:47:59,076 --> 01:48:00,406
Come on, son.

947
01:48:02,246 --> 01:48:03,735
Come on up outa there.

948
01:49:07,343 --> 01:49:08,674
I got my mind right.

949
01:49:45,047 --> 01:49:46,207
Where are you?

950
01:49:48,050 --> 01:49:49,539
Where are you now?

951
01:50:36,732 --> 01:50:40,223
-All right. Smoke it up. -Yes, sir.

952
01:50:42,436 --> 01:50:44,427
Luke, water 'em down.

953
01:50:46,140 --> 01:50:47,232
Yes, Boss.

954
01:51:09,297 --> 01:51:11,288
Luke! Fetch the rifle.

955
01:52:01,848 --> 01:52:03,008
You got him, Boss. You got him.

956
01:52:04,184 --> 01:52:05,514
Go fetch it, Luke.

957
01:52:26,206 --> 01:52:29,038
There he is, Boss. Deader than hell, but won't let go.

958
01:52:39,551 --> 01:52:41,381
You cut that up for our lunch, Luke.

959
01:52:43,323 --> 01:52:45,153
Yes, Boss Paul.

960
01:53:31,437 --> 01:53:33,927
He took the keys off of Dogboy's truck.

961
01:53:34,939 --> 01:53:36,769
He got the keys here, too.

962
01:53:53,124 --> 01:53:56,286
"I'm shaking it here, Boss. I'm shaking it."

963
01:54:02,467 --> 01:54:04,127
That's my baby, Luke.

964
01:54:07,638 --> 01:54:10,801
"Don't hit me, Boss. Only don't hit me.

965
01:54:11,809 --> 01:54:13,469
"I'll do whatever you say."

966
01:54:15,813 --> 01:54:18,373
You are an original, that's what you are.

967
01:54:18,449 --> 01:54:21,144
Those mullet-heads didn't even know you were fooling.

968
01:54:22,987 --> 01:54:26,581
Fooling them? You can't fool them about something like that.

969
01:54:26,656 --> 01:54:27,713
They broke me.

970
01:54:29,160 --> 01:54:31,821
But they didn't get my mind right. Not with no sticks. No, sir.

971
01:54:33,497 --> 01:54:35,829
All that time you were planning on running again.

972
01:54:37,168 --> 01:54:39,158
Never planned anything in my life.

973
01:55:05,529 --> 01:55:08,361
That's just a little old farm road. Clean as a whistle.

974
01:55:08,698 --> 01:55:12,030
I worked it a couple times. We're home free. Come on.

975
01:55:12,369 --> 01:55:13,529
We ain't going nowhere.

976
01:55:13,637 --> 01:55:15,331
Now, what are you talking about, Luke?

977
01:55:15,871 --> 01:55:18,532
We're going by my house and we're going to have a big meal.

978
01:55:18,874 --> 01:55:23,208
Then I'm going to show you a couple of farm girls that really know what fun...

979
01:55:24,548 --> 01:55:26,208
And then we're going to get Koko out of there.

980
01:55:26,550 --> 01:55:29,211
And then the terrible trio is gonna be complete again.

981
01:55:29,286 --> 01:55:32,584
Man, this old free world ain't going to know which ear to stand on.

982
01:55:33,722 --> 01:55:36,714
Yeah, well, you and Koko can handle it without me.

983
01:55:38,028 --> 01:55:40,018
What's you mean, Luke?

984
01:55:40,397 --> 01:55:42,227
I done enough world-shaking for a while.

985
01:55:42,566 --> 01:55:45,557
You do the rest of it for me. Send me a postcard about it.

986
01:55:45,801 --> 01:55:47,359
-But Luke... -Take it easy, Drag.

987
01:55:47,903 --> 01:55:48,892
Where are you going?

988
01:55:49,905 --> 01:55:51,132
Just on my own.

989
01:55:52,575 --> 01:55:55,236
But what am I going to do all by myself?

990
01:55:57,746 --> 01:56:01,079
Man, if I hadn't lost my head. I only had a couple of years to do.

991
01:56:02,417 --> 01:56:05,580
But when I saw you tearing down the road in that truck...

992
01:56:08,924 --> 01:56:10,584
Well, you're right, Luke.

993
01:56:11,927 --> 01:56:13,587
We ought to split up.

994
01:56:14,263 --> 01:56:18,062
And then, and then it will be safer for the both of us.

995
01:56:23,271 --> 01:56:26,263
Just the same, you're a good old boy, Luke.

996
01:56:29,611 --> 01:56:30,942
You take care!

997
01:57:28,201 --> 01:57:29,532
Anybody here?

998
01:57:45,218 --> 01:57:47,048
Hey, Old Man. You home tonight?

999
01:57:52,559 --> 01:57:55,550
Can You spare a minute. It's about time we had a little talk.

1000
01:58:00,067 --> 01:58:01,897
I know I'm a pretty evil fellow...

1001
01:58:02,737 --> 01:58:06,069
...killed people in the war and got drunk...

1002
01:58:06,907 --> 01:58:09,000
...and chewed up municipal property and the like.

1003
01:58:09,142 --> 01:58:11,109
I know I got no call to ask for much...

1004
01:58:11,244 --> 01:58:14,406
...but even so, You've got to admit You ain't dealt me no cards in a long time.

1005
01:58:17,250 --> 01:58:20,582
It's beginning to look like You got things fixed so I can't never win out.

1006
01:58:22,422 --> 01:58:23,581
Inside, outside, all of them...

1007
01:58:25,158 --> 01:58:28,649
...rules and regulations and bosses.

1008
01:58:28,729 --> 01:58:30,559
You made me like I am.

1009
01:58:30,897 --> 01:58:33,092
Now just where am I supposed to fit in?

1010
01:58:36,103 --> 01:58:38,935
Old Man, I gotta tell You.

1011
01:58:40,773 --> 01:58:43,105
I started out pretty strong and fast.

1012
01:58:47,780 --> 01:58:49,440
But it's beginning to get to me.

1013
01:58:52,451 --> 01:58:53,611
When does it end?

1014
01:58:55,454 --> 01:58:57,114
What do You got in mind for me?

1015
01:58:58,290 --> 01:58:59,779
What do I do now?

1016
01:59:14,974 --> 01:59:16,463
On my knees, asking.

1017
01:59:29,154 --> 01:59:30,814
Yeah, that's what I thought.

1018
01:59:33,324 --> 01:59:35,315
I guess I'm pretty tough to deal with?

1019
01:59:36,829 --> 01:59:38,318
A hard case.

1020
01:59:41,667 --> 01:59:43,634
Guess I gotta find my own way.

1021
02:00:08,493 --> 02:00:10,153
Is that Your answer, Old Man?

1022
02:00:12,697 --> 02:00:14,688
I guess You're a hard case, too.

1023
02:00:20,205 --> 02:00:22,195
Luke, you all right?

1024
02:00:24,375 --> 02:00:28,207
They got us, boy. They're out there, thicker than flies.

1025
02:00:28,880 --> 02:00:30,871
Bosses, dogs, sheriffs...

1026
02:00:31,216 --> 02:00:34,207
...more guns than I've ever seen in my life. You ain't got a chance.

1027
02:00:34,551 --> 02:00:37,212
They caught up with me right after we split up.

1028
02:00:37,721 --> 02:00:41,212
And they were aiming to kill you. But I fixed that.

1029
02:00:41,892 --> 02:00:44,883
I got them to promise if you give up peaceful...

1030
02:00:45,729 --> 02:00:47,889
...they ain't even going to whip you this time.

1031
02:00:49,733 --> 02:00:52,223
They even going to give us our same bunks back?

1032
02:00:52,569 --> 02:00:54,399
Sure, why not?

1033
02:00:54,738 --> 02:00:58,901
We only been gone a couple of hours. They're reasonable men.

1034
02:01:08,252 --> 02:01:09,912
You've got to listen to me.

1035
02:01:11,255 --> 02:01:14,588
All you've got to do is give up...

1036
02:01:15,259 --> 02:01:16,590
...nice and quiet.

1037
02:01:17,928 --> 02:01:19,757
Just play it cool.

1038
02:01:22,766 --> 02:01:24,289
Yeah, like I always do?

1039
02:01:24,868 --> 02:01:26,630
Yeah, just play it...

1040
02:01:55,131 --> 02:01:58,964
"What we got here is a failure to communicate."

1041
02:02:42,677 --> 02:02:43,665
Go get him.

1042
02:03:20,881 --> 02:03:24,078
You hang on in there, Luke. You hang on.

1043
02:03:26,221 --> 02:03:29,053
There's going to be some world-shaking, Luke.

1044
02:03:30,392 --> 02:03:32,382
We're going to send you a postcard.

1045
02:03:34,061 --> 02:03:36,551
You follow me and I'll radio the emergency clinic to open up.

1046
02:03:36,897 --> 02:03:38,888
I'm taking him to the prison hospital.

1047
02:03:39,099 --> 02:03:40,964
But that's an hour away. He isn't going to make it.

1048
02:03:41,068 --> 02:03:42,898
Get out of the way. He's ours.

1049
02:04:28,582 --> 02:04:30,674
They took him right down that road.

1050
02:04:30,951 --> 02:04:33,441
-What'd he look like, Drag? -Yeah, Drag.

1051
02:04:33,954 --> 02:04:35,682
Did he have his eyes open or closed?

1052
02:04:35,789 --> 02:04:38,313
-He was smiling. -Smiling?!

1053
02:04:40,193 --> 02:04:41,489
That's right. You know...

1054
02:04:43,163 --> 02:04:44,823
...that...Luke smile of his?

1055
02:04:45,631 --> 02:04:47,791
He had it on his face right to the very end.

1056
02:04:48,301 --> 02:04:49,268
Hell, if they didn't know it 'fore...

1057
02:04:49,336 --> 02:04:52,133
...they could tell right then that they weren't ever going to beat him.

1058
02:04:54,140 --> 02:04:55,629
That old Luke smile.

1059
02:04:58,010 --> 02:05:01,672
Oh, Luke. He was some boy.

1060
02:05:01,848 --> 02:05:03,906
Cool Hand Luke, hell!

1061
02:05:04,083 --> 02:05:06,244
He's a natural born world-shaker!

